{"url": "https://github.com/duongtran14/Partial-replication-of-Gu-Kelly-Xiu-2020-Empirical-Asset-Pricing-via-Machine-Learning.", "title": "duongtran14/Partial-replication-of-Gu-Kelly-Xiu-2020-Empirical-Asset-Pricing-via-Machine-Learning.", "engine": "exa", "published": "N/A", "snippet": "Replication of the paper Empirical Asset Pricing via Machine Learning by Gu, Kelly, & Xiu (2020). Neural networks with 3 hidden layers are used to predict 35 years of US stock returns.\n...\nThis is my own attempt to replicate some of the key findings in the paper Empirical Asset Pricing via Machine Learning by Gu, Kelly, &amp; Xiu (2020)[^1]. Here, I use **neural networks with 3 hidden layers** (\"NN3\") to predict US stock excess returns and evaluate the model's performance for the period **1987-2021, i.e 35-year out-of-sample testing** (1987-2016 in the original paper). The paper, using a total of **920 baseline predictors** (including 94 stock-level characteristics, 8 macro-economic predictors), has shown that machine learning models, notably trees and neural networks, are very promising for algorithmic trading strategies and can yield large economic gains to investors, demonstrated by a high out-of-sample $R^2$ and Sharpe ratio using a decile-sorted machine learning portfolio strategy compared to existing literature and other simple regression-based methods.\n...\n- `1_Preprocessing.ipynb`: Download raw data and compute input data for model training, validation, and testing;\n...\n- `2_NN3.ipynb`: Use 3-hidden-layer neural networks to train, validate, and generate excess return predictions for each year from 1987-2021;\n- `3_PortfPerformance_replicated.ipynb`: Decile-sort stocks based on their return predictions and adopt a zero-net (dollar-neutral) investment strategy: long high", "extra": {}, "read_via": "direct", "text_chars": 10760, "excerpt": "This is my own attempt to replicate some of the key findings in the paper Empirical Asset Pricing via Machine Learning by Gu, Kelly, & Xiu (2020)1. Here, I use neural networks with 3 hidden layers (\"NN3\") to predict US stock excess returns and evaluate the model's performance for the period 1987-2021, i.e 35-year out-of-sample testing (1987-2016 in the original paper). The paper, using a total of ", "jev": {"concrete": 0.91, "evidence": "backtest", "evidence_confidence": 1.0, "market": "us_stocks_etfs", "us_long_only": 0.27, "recent": 0.01, "code": 0.93}, "priority": 0.651}
